{"id":"beriah","name":"Beriah","aliases":[],"sources":["nave","easton"],"topics":["nave:beriah"],"groups":[],"definition":{"source":"easton","term":"Beriah","text":"A gift, or in evil. (1.) One of Asher’s four sons, and father of Heber (Gen. 46:17). (2.) A son of Ephraim (1 Chr. 7:20-23), born after the slaughter of his brothers, and so called by his father “because it went evil with his house” at that time. (3.) A Benjamite who with his brother Shema founded Ajalon and expelled the Gittites (1 Chr. 8:13)."},"lemmas":[{"strong":"H1283","lemma":"בְּרִיעָה","xlit":"Bᵉrîyʻâh","gloss":"Beriah, the name of four Israelites","kjv":"Beriah","count":8,"share":0.73},{"strong":"H3232","lemma":"יִמְנָה","xlit":"Yimnâh","gloss":"Jimnah, the name of two Israelites","kjv":"Imna, Imnah, Jimnah, Jimnites","count":3,"share":0.27},{"strong":"H3440","lemma":"יִשְׁוִי","xlit":"Yishvîy","gloss":"Jishvi, the name of two Israelites","kjv":"Ishuai, Ishvi, Isui, Jesui","count":3,"share":0.27},{"strong":"H836","lemma":"אָשֵׁר","xlit":"ʼÂshêr","gloss":"happy","kjv":"Asher","count":3,"share":0.27},{"strong":"H3438","lemma":"יִשְׁוָה","xlit":"Yishvâh","gloss":"Jishvah, an Israelite","kjv":"Ishvah, Isvah","count":2,"share":0.18},{"strong":"H8294","lemma":"שֶׂרַח","xlit":"Serach","gloss":"Serach, an Israelitess","kjv":"Sarah, Serah","count":2,"share":0.18}],"verses":["Gen.46.17","Num.26.44","Num.26.45","1Chr.7.23","1Chr.7.30","1Chr.8.13","1Chr.23.10","1Chr.23.11","1Chr.7.20","1Chr.7.21","1Chr.7.22"],"related":[{"id":"ishui","type":"cooccur","shared":3,"jaccard":0.25,"why":"3 verses are indexed under both"},{"id":"asher","type":"cooccur","shared":3,"jaccard":0.071,"why":"3 verses are indexed under both"},{"id":"asher-the-tribe-of","type":"cooccur","shared":3,"jaccard":0.049,"why":"3 verses are indexed under both"},{"id":"ephraim","type":"cooccur","shared":4,"jaccard":0.03,"why":"4 verses are indexed under both"},{"id":"malchiel","type":"lexical","strong":"H1283","why":"both lead with בְּרִיעָה (H12